§5 ⚜ ᴀ ꜱᴛᴏʀʏ ꜱᴇʀɪᴇꜱ ⚜
#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2        ᴛʜᴇ ᴄᴏᴅᴇ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2Fern, now a renowned warrior with her enchanted blade The Soultrap, found herself wandering through the dense land's of Craftadia. She had heard rumors of a place called 
The End, a very mysterious realm...
#- §2On a misty morning, while taking shelter at an old Tavern called The Spyglass, her path crossed with that of Castien, a Mage with eyes that shimmered like the stars. He was searching for his Emerald Crown, stolen by an unknown thief. Their meeting was not by chance. Both had been drawn here by
#- §2whispers of Azarla, a mighty dragon whose reign of terror had spread far and wide. Together, they ventured into old ruins, guided there by coordinates the thief strangly left behind. They found The Emerald Crown, but so much more; The End. 
A place where reality twisted and time
#- §2stood still. Castien's magic complemented Fern's swordsmanship perfectly. With each clash against Azarla, their bond grew stronger. The dragon's fiery breath and titanic strength were formidable, but it was the combined might of Fern’s blade and Castien’s spells that finally brought
#- §2the beast down. The moment Azarla fell, a new legend was born!

Word of their heroic deed spread quickly throughout Craftadia. Songs were sung, and tales were told of Fern and Castien. Mainly by wandering witches' like me. Fame brought them closer, and their shared
#- §2adventures turned into a deep and abiding love. Under a sky lit by a thousand stars, they pledged their lives to each other, sealing their bond in a celebration that united warriors, mages, and common folk alike. Yet, as Fern dreamed of a quiet life away from battles and quests,
#- §2Castien's heart burned with an insatiable hunger for more. He was drawn to the power he believed still lay hidden in the ancient texts and artefacts scattered across Craftadia.  Every day, he grew more obsessed, pouring over scrolls and deciphering cryptic maps.
#- §2Fern watched in silence, her worry growing with each passing moment. 
As months turned into years, Castien's behavior became increasingly erratic. He disappeared for days, sometimes weeks. Fern tried to reach him, but Castien was consumed by his quest. He spoke of
#- §2a §8code§2. A §8code §2that could reshape the very fabric of reality. Fern's quiet concern turned to fear. She noticed the darkening of Castien’s aura, the cold detachment in his voice. She yearned to confront him, to ask him to abandon his perilous path, but love held her tongue. 
One stormy night,  
#- §2Castien stumbled home, and Fern could feel him wrapped in a sinister energy. Fern could no longer stay silent. "Castien, this madness will destroy us both," she implored, her voice trembling. "Please, stop before it’s too late." But Castien shook his head. "§cI cannot stop, this power... it could
#- §cchange everything§2!"

Fern’s heart ached as she saw the man she loved slipping away. She resolved to stay by his side, hoping against all hope that love might yet save him from himself. She faced the greatest battle of all; saving the soul of 
the man she loved!
#- §2To be continued…
§5✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿

§2Tune in next time 
for more of... 
ꜰᴇʀɴ'ꜱ ᴀᴅᴠᴇɴᴛᴜʀᴇꜱ!

Read previous stories in the previous issues!
